     <div class="sec-head"><p class="kicker">FAQ</p><h2>Questions, answered</h2></div>
     <div class="faq">
       <details open><summary>Is Penwright really free?</summary><p>Yes. There are no accounts, watermarks or page limits. Everything runs in your browser, so there’s nothing to pay for on our side.</p></details>
+      <details><summary>Can I install it on my computer or phone?</summary><p>Yes. Click <b>Install app</b> at the top of the page. In Chrome or Edge (Windows, Mac, Linux, ChromeOS, Android) Penwright installs in one click. On iPhone and iPad use Share, then Add to Home Screen; in Safari on a Mac use File, then Add to Dock. It opens in its own window with its own icon, and keeps working with no internet. You can also open Word, PDF and text files with it straight from your file manager.</p></details>
       <details><summary>Can I use my own handwriting?</summary><p>Yes. Create a font from a photo of your handwriting with a free tool like Calligraphr, then upload the .ttf/.otf in the <em>Hand</em> tab. Penwright applies all the same natural variation to it, and remembers it on this device.</p></details>
       <details><summary>Will it print at the right size?</summary><p>PDFs are generated at the exact paper size (US Letter, A4, A5, Legal, index card or sticky note). Choose “Digital” finish and print at 100% / actual size for the most natural result on real paper.</p></details>
